    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="0877" n="865" xml:id="pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/769½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to Mr. Wright Thomas of the Division of Exports and
                        Defense Aid</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-26">December 26, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Thank you very much for sending me a copy of the draft agreement<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d814-f1"/> which I am holding for the time being. In regard to that
                    section relative to the protection of patent rights, we believe that a
                    consideration which should be borne in mind is that the Soviet Government has
                    not hesitated in the past arbitrarily to copy any patented machine or article
                    imported into the Soviet Union without paying any attention to the foreign
                    patentee. There is no reason to believe that the Soviet Government would not
                    continue this practice in the future and would not hesitate to export articles
                    patented in the United States but manufactured in the Soviet Union.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oy</hi>] W. H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >enderson</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d814-f1" n="42" xml:id="d814-f1-content">
                <p>Draft of a lend-lease agreement between the United States and the Soviet Union,
                    not attached to the memorandum.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
